@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Daily Grind Web Components
+
+Load `components/index.js` once with a `<script type="module">`. Components use
+open Shadow DOM, shared parsed templates, and native links/buttons. No build
+step or framework is required. Their content is authored in light DOM so links
+and headings remain available if JavaScript fails.
+
+| Element | Slots | Styling hooks |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `coffee-card` | `heading` (h2/h3 as appropriate), `description` (p), `action` (a) | `--card-background`, `--primary`, `--text`; `::part(card)` |
+| `coffee-hero` | `heading`, `description`, `action` | `--hero-image` (CSS image value), `--primary`, `--text`; `::part(hero)` |
+| `site-navigation` | `brand`, default (direct a children) | `--primary`, `--accent`; `.logout-link` on a slotted link |
+| `site-footer` | default (direct a children), `copyright` | `--secondary`, `--text`; `::part(footer)` |
+
+Theme variables inherit from the document or an ancestor, with component-local
+fallback values. Slots style direct children only. Keep content in slot order
+for a consistent reading order. Provide descriptive action link text or an
+`aria-label` including the visible link text and the coffee name.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card>
+  <h3 slot="heading">House Blend</h3>
+  <p slot="description">A balanced everyday roast.</p>
+  <a slot="action" href="/menu/house-blend">Explore House Blend</a>
+</coffee-card>
+```
+
+The navigation uses ordinary links and a native disclosure button below 48rem.
+Enter/Space toggle it; Tab follows the normal document order; Escape closes it
+and returns focus to the button. Desktop links are always available. Listeners
+are removed when disconnected and restored when reconnected. The disclosure's
+ARIA relationship stays entirely inside its shadow root.
+
+Page-level CSS owns layout and the no-JavaScript fallback. Component CSS owns
+internal layout, controls, focus indicators, and theming. The homepage retains
+all existing route destinations; this refactor does not implement those routes.
